# ============================================================================
# coconut_quadplane.param
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ArduPilot QuadPlane parameter overlay for the coconut-surveillance airframe.
#
# Airframe (finalized spec, see documents/quadplane_roadmap_2.md):
#   - 4x A2212 2200KV lift motors, standard quad-X
#   - 1x A2212 2200KV forward/cruise motor (nose or pusher)
#   - 2x elevons (combined pitch + roll); NO separate aileron/elevator/rudder
#     control surface. Fixed horizontal tail + twin fins are passive only.
#   - 5x SimonK 30A ESCs
#
# HOW TO LOAD (in the MAVProxy console that sim_vehicle.py opens):
#   param load /mnt/e/proggramming/semester proj/flight_software/coconut_quadplane.param
#   param fetch
#   reboot
# or in Mission Planner: CONFIG > Full Parameter List > Load from file.
#
# Load this AFTER the vehicle has booted once with `-f quadplane` so the
# quadplane.parm defaults are already in place; this file only sets the
# deltas that make the sim match our airframe.
# ============================================================================

# --- QuadPlane core ---------------------------------------------------------
Q_ENABLE          1        # QuadPlane subsystem on
Q_FRAME_CLASS     1        # 1 = Quad
Q_FRAME_TYPE      1        # 1 = X  (standard quad-X)
Q_TILT_MASK       0        # nothing tilts (pure quadplane, not tiltrotor)

# --- Servo / motor output mapping -----------------------------------------
# Plane control surfaces on outputs 1-4, VTOL motors on 5-8 (ArduPilot's
# recommended standard ordering). We replace aileron+elevator with elevons.
SERVO1_FUNCTION   77       # Elevon Left
SERVO2_FUNCTION   78       # Elevon Right
SERVO3_FUNCTION   70       # Throttle  -> forward/cruise motor
SERVO4_FUNCTION   0        # disabled (no rudder surface on this airframe)
SERVO5_FUNCTION   33       # Motor 1  (front-right, CCW)
SERVO6_FUNCTION   34       # Motor 2  (rear-left,  CCW)
SERVO7_FUNCTION   35       # Motor 3  (front-left, CW)
SERVO8_FUNCTION   36       # Motor 4  (rear-right, CW)

# ESC PWM band for SimonK 30A (calibrate on real hardware later)
SERVO5_MIN        1000
SERVO5_MAX        2000
SERVO6_MIN        1000
SERVO6_MAX        2000
SERVO7_MIN        1000
SERVO7_MAX        2000
SERVO8_MIN        1000
SERVO8_MAX        2000

# --- Elevon mixing --------------------------------------------------------
MIXING_GAIN       0.5      # roll/pitch blend into the two elevons; retune in flight
MIXING_OFFSET     0        # keep roll/pitch authority symmetric to start

# --- Motor behaviour -----------------------------------------------------
Q_M_PWM_MIN       1000
Q_M_PWM_MAX       2000
Q_M_SPIN_ARM      0.10     # idle-spin when armed
Q_M_SPIN_MIN      0.15     # min commanded thrust
Q_M_SPIN_MAX      0.95
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX  12.6     # 3S nominal fully charged
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN  9.9      # 3S cutoff (3.3 V/cell)

# --- Transition / VTOL assist ------------------------------------------
Q_ASSIST_SPEED    9        # m/s: below this, lift motors assist fixed-wing flight
Q_ASSIST_ANGLE    30       # deg attitude error that also triggers assist
Q_TRANSITION_MS   5000     # max ms to reach AIRSPEED_MIN before forcing transition
Q_RTL_MODE        1        # do a VTOL landing at end of RTL

# --- Fixed-wing envelope (small foam wing, 1.3 m span) ----------------
# ArduPlane 4.5+ names: AIRSPEED_* in m/s (older ARSPD_FBW_* / TRIM_ARSPD_CM gone)
# Cruise refined 16 -> 12 m/s: the aero analysis (aero/RESULTS.md, wing
# incidence 1 deg) shows this light wing trims at negative alpha above ~13 m/s.
# 3D CLmax ~1.33 -> Vstall ~7.5 m/s at 1.4 kg AUW, so AIRSPEED_MIN 9 = ~1.2 Vs.
AIRSPEED_MIN      9        # m/s, ~1.2x stall
AIRSPEED_MAX      22
AIRSPEED_CRUISE   12       # cruise target, m/s  (was 16)
SCALING_SPEED     12
WP_RADIUS         25       # m: waypoint acceptance radius for AUTO nav
WP_LOITER_RAD     40       # m: ~turn radius at 12 m/s, 25 deg bank (~31 m) + margin

# --- Battery / failsafe (simulation-safe starting values) --------------
BATT_MONITOR      4        # analog volt+current (sim provides this)
BATT_CAPACITY     5000
BATT_LOW_VOLT     10.2
BATT_CRT_VOLT     9.9
FS_LONG_ACTN      1        # RTL on long failsafe

# --- Notes --------------------------------------------------------------
# * Transition tuning (Q_TRANS_*, Q_WVANE_*, TECS_*) is intentionally left at
#   defaults here — tune only after basic hover + a clean forward transition
#   are confirmed in SITL.
# * The SITL aero model is ArduPilot's GENERIC quadplane, not our wing/airfoil.
#   A JSBSim model built from the chosen airfoil (see
#   documents/airframe_tail_airfoil_decision.md) is later work.
